From c63558e9e9550ff59737ab8790c87cf3780c0e67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: op-bench-framework <op-bench-framework@pypto-x.local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 05:37:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 217/235] fix(op-bench): session hygiene + report provenance
 follow-ups

D-3 follow-up (verifier finding): the test file no longer mutates the
session at all.
- remove the module-level os.environ.setdefault('PYPTO_X_PORTABLE_ONLY')
  (it forced portable-only mode on classic sessions); import the real pypto
  package and run in whatever mode the session started with;
- when pypto is not importable at all (source tree, no env, no wheel) skip
  the module explicitly instead of fabricating a module;
- the guard test is now mode-agnostic (real module, __portable_only__
  attribute present, real pypto.op_bench submodule; portable branch only when
  the session is portable-only) and a subprocess test proves the import does
  not change PYPTO_X_PORTABLE_ONLY.

Verifier non-blocking items:
- artifacts: embedded sha256 map now excludes the report JSON itself (a file
  cannot embed its own final hash); every embedded digest equals the bytes on
  disk and sha256sums.txt carries the true report hash. Existing reports were
  refreshed in place without re-measurement (logs/refresh_reports.py);
- status_reason is filter-aware: the repro report now says
  'measured 2/19 cases; 17 explicitly skipped by --case-filter' and the main
  report 'measured 32/53 cases; 7 explicit not_run_budget case(s)';
- host_fingerprint records python_executable and numpy; both drivers pin the
  interpreter PATH (x86 miniforge bin; A3 dirname of the selected python);
- refresh the committed report samples and their hashes.
